        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Paint Sprayer Rental", item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/paint-sprayer-rental/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Should I rent or buy a paint sprayer?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Rent if you have a single project under 800 square feet of surface area, will use the sprayer once, and don't want to handle ongoing maintenance. Buy if you'll do multiple projects in 1-2 years, your project exceeds 1,500 square feet, or you want a sprayer always available for touch-ups. The break-even point is approximately 2-3 rental days against the cost of a Graco Magnum X7.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does it cost to rent a paint sprayer?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "At big-box retailers (Home Depot, Lowe's): $60-80 for 4 hours, $80-100 for 24 hours, $300-350 for a week. At pro rental chains (Sunbelt, United Rentals): $120-160 for 4 hours, $180-240 for 24 hours. Local paint stores often offer competitive rates, especially bundled with paint purchases.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What happens if I return a rental sprayer dirty?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Most rental companies charge a cleaning fee of $50-100 if the sprayer is returned with paint residue inside the pump, hose, or gun. Big-box retailers enforce this strictly. The cleaning fee can exceed half the original rental cost, so allocate 30-45 minutes for proper cleanup before returning. Bring the sprayer back disassembled and visibly clean if possible.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do I need to bring my own paint to a rental?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, paint sprayer rentals do not include paint. You provide your own paint, primer, thinner, and cleaning supplies. The rental typically includes the sprayer, hose, gun, one spray tip, and basic accessories. Specialty tips, brushes, filters, and cleaning chemicals are extra.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I rent a paint sprayer overnight?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, most rental companies offer 24-hour rental periods that allow overnight use. Home Depot's 24-hour rental typically runs $80-100. The 24-hour option is usually better value than the 4-hour rental for any project where you might lose track of time — a 5-hour project on a 4-hour rental can become more expensive than the 24-hour option due to overage charges.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Alex Rivers" },
